{
  "id": "the-stale-record",
  "name": "The Stale Record",
  "category": "services",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "xp": 250,
  "level": 6,
  "description": "The name resolves. The address it gives is wrong.",
  "brief": "🚨 SERVICE DOWN\n\nNobody can load web.netquest.local. DNS is clearly working — every lookup gets a prompt answer with no errors at all.\n\nThe answer is simply not true. Find out what the web server's address actually is, then compare it with what DNS is handing out.",
  "hints": [
    "Run 'nslookup web.netquest.local' on PC-01. Note the address.",
    "Now select WEB-01 and look at the address it really has.",
    "Try pinging both addresses and see which one answers.",
    "Fix the A record on DNS-01 so it points at the real server."
  ],
  "explanation": "A successful lookup is not the same as a correct one. DNS answered every query without complaint, so nothing in the output looked like an error — it was simply pointing at an address where nothing lived.\n\nThis is why the habit of checking what a name resolves to, and then checking that address separately, matters so much. 'NXDOMAIN' is easy to spot; a confidently wrong answer is not.",
